-- #1111 A-2.5b (#1275) — THE SEVERITY-MIRROR ACCEPT CELL: a VALID program that the
-- pre-fix compiler REJECTED.  `exit 1 → exit 0` is the transition AGENTS.md warns is
-- untested by construction (every pre-existing fixture covered the rejecting case),
-- so this asserts the RUNTIME VALUE, on all three engines, not just silence.
--
-- EXPECTED VALUE DERIVED BY HAND from the language semantics, not captured from an
-- engine: `msmth` reaches this module only through `msmid`, which re-exports
-- `msifb`'s, so the occurrence means `MSIB.msmth`.  This module implements exactly
-- that interface (`MSIB` is the name `msmid` re-exports; `msbys`'s same-named `MSIB`
-- is not in scope here at all).  The program is well typed and must print `B`.
--
-- 🚨 BEFORE A-2.5b this was REJECTED, `No impl of MSIA for Blob` — a FALSE REJECT of
-- a valid program, citing an interface the call never names, caused entirely by the
-- bystander `msbys`.  Rename `msbys`'s interface to `MSIZ` and the PRE-FIX compiler
-- accepted this same file: that one identifier, in a module this entry neither
-- imports nor mentions, was the whole difference.  Measured on `main` @ ae39ec41.
--
-- Its rejecting mirrors are `analyze_project_fixtures/1275_bystander_iface_name_
-- method_scope` (same graph, impl on the WRONG interface — must still reject) and
-- `.../1275_genuine_error_under_bystander` (no impl at all — must still reject).
import msmid.{MSIB, msmth}
import msifa.{MSIA}

data Blob = Blob

impl MSIB Blob where
  msmth _ = "B"

main : <IO> Unit
main = putStrLn (msmth Blob)
